    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0123" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/3722</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 9.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is intention of British authorities to accept manufactures of rubber for
                    shipment via Halifax as satisfying undertaking of American concerns to ship
                    rubber goods only via United Kingdom provided that in all cases such shipments
                    must be made under special licenses to be issued by British Embassy as in case
                    of ordinary shipments to Scandinavia. Applications for these licenses will be
                    considered in usual way and subject to all conditions which affect granting of
                    export licenses in United Kingdom.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
